  "comment": "60-DEGREE RHOMBUS BUBBLE TILES, the 2-iamond family (Chase, Field & McCluer Appendix B, Figure 27). A rhombus is equilateral but NOT regular: the angle word is (60,120,60,120), period 2, so a bite word is canonical up to rotation by two and the family is (2^4 + 2^2)/2 = 10 tiles, not the square's 6. Three of the ten are chiral partners of another three (the paper's 1*, 2A*, 3*); the engine cannot place a tile reflected, so each is its own alphabet symbol and both are listed. Angles in D=24 units: 60 = 4, 120 = 8, so a vertex is any multiset of 4s and 8s summing to 24 - valence 3 to 6.",
